---
title: "Life OS: one task's Google Calendar event"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: settled
    lg1: waiting
    lg2: stuck
    lg3: Breaks RateLimitIsRetried or UnwantedEventLeaves or WantedEventArrives
    lg4: Breaks RateLimitIsRetried in some cases
    lg5: Path to the RateLimitIsRetried or UnwantedEventLeaves or WantedEventArrives bug
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 orange
  class lg3 breaks
  class lg4 mayBreak
  class lg5 bugPath
  s0: Not on the calendar
  s1: Waiting to be added
  s2: Rate limited, nothing retries
  s3: On the calendar
  s4: Waiting to be removed
  s5: Marked deleted in Google
  s6: Left behind in Google
  s7: Missing, nothing adds it
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s0: you give it a date or you turn auto-add on or you turn sync on or the push runs
  s0 --> s1: you turn sync on or you give it a date or you turn auto-add on
  s1 --> s0: you turn sync off or you take the date away or you turn auto-add off
  s1 --> s2: Google rate-limits
  s1 --> s3: the push runs or you press Repair
  s2 --> s3: you press Repair or you give it a date
  s2 --> s1: you turn auto-add on or you turn sync on or you give it a date
  s3 --> s4: you turn sync off or you take the date away or you turn auto-add off
  s3 --> s5: it is gone in Google
  s3 --> s2: Google rate-limits
  s4 --> s0: the cleanup runs or you press Repair or the push runs
  s4 --> s6: Google refuses
  s0 --> s7: you turn sync on
  s5 --> s3: you press Repair
  s2 --> s4: you turn sync off or you take the date away or you turn auto-add off or you give it a date
  s5 --> s0: you turn auto-add off or the push runs
  s4 --> s3: you give it a date or you turn auto-add on or Google refuses or you turn sync on
  s4 --> s2: Google rate-limits or the cleanup runs or Google refuses
  s6 --> s3: you turn sync on or you turn auto-add on or you give it a date
  s6 --> s4: you take the date away or you turn sync off or you give it a date or you turn auto-add off
  s4 --> s1: the cleanup runs
  s7 --> s0: you take the date away or you turn sync off or you turn auto-add off
  s7 --> s3: you press Repair
  s7 --> s1: you turn auto-add on
  s5 --> s1: you give it a date
  s2 --> s0: you press Repair
  s6 --> s0: you press Repair
  s1 --> s4: you press Repair
  s1 --> s7: Google refuses
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
